			<div class="content" id="post-content-1703907">
									

<p>Addressing these concerns in order: (will address other ones when they appear and when I return)</p>
<p>1. In retrospect, &quot;wear-and-tear&quot; does appear to be somewhat out of place. I have changed it to &quot;mishandling&quot;, which would probably where most of the damage would probably come from in the first place.<br />
2. &quot;Carbon dated&quot; is an actual way to refer to an item that has been radio-carbon tested.<br />
3. I agree that this is a very bad wording, and it has been changed to something more indicative of their positioning.<br />
4. I used this method of discovery because I had seen it on other SCPs in the past. For example, both <a href="/scp-1733">SCP-1733</a> and <a href="/scp-261">SCP-261</a> used similar discovery stories.<br />
5. Reading through it, I think the last sentence was probably the most problematic one. Changed it to &quot;a dead body seated in the chair&quot;, which sounds more natural.</p>

