<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Storage Site-23 was chosen to be the destination of the object after extraterrestrial retrieval, due to general proximity and its standard storage chambers being suitable for its containment.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I dont't know if this is needed.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After it was brought to Storage Site-23, the body was taken away and brought to the medical wing for an autopsy</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Now, it sounds like you're telling a story. You know the &quot;And then this happened&quot; kind of story.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>At the same time, Mr. C████ had been contacted as an outside expert on his subject and was asked to give an inspection of the object based on his expertise.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>See above post.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He had inferred correctly that the piece dated from the Ming Dynasty and noted the damage the object had received, then suggested measures that could restore the object and preserve it in the long-term.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Now, I know SCPs are supposed to tell stories, but not in the same style as you would find in a book.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Based on his knowledge and skill in his field of expertise, he was hired shortly afterwards and inducted as a curator for SCP-1445, and has since led the effort in preserving the object.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You already said he was an expert.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Upon detailed examination of the retrieved objects by scientific personnel, it was noted that neither the chair nor the body suffered the damage that they should have sustained upon traveling at escape velocity from atmospheric friction and drag.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Scientific personnel? Makes me think this: The Foundation personnel run around everywhere bopping people on the head with foam bats, screaming &quot;For Science!&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The body was noted to be wearing a hanfu appropriate to the style of the Ming Dynasty and a wushamao3, providing further evidence of the object's time of origin.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You already said it was from the Ming Dynasty. Why bother repeating yourself?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>he specimen also appeared to have suffered from micrometeoroid damage like the chair also had.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Bad tone.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A testing procedure for SCP-1445 has been proposed by Dr. A███, in order to discern the anomalous properties of the object directly through experimentation. After consultation with other departments of the Foundation and a week of consideration, the proposal was denied by Site Director ██████.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Wait&#8230; We don't even know what this thing does? For all we know, this may be an elaborate hoax.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The fuses of the object are capable of regeneration. The object was found with fuses whole and unburnt, but contemporary documents clearly describe a &quot;[…] ceremonious lighting of the fuses&quot;.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So regenerating fuses? That's only an Anomalous Object, not an SCP.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The addendum.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah, we don't need this. It serves no purpose to the article. It also could be considered a form of LoLFoundation.</p>
